INT. TUGBOAT CABIN - NIGHT

PRE-LAP: a foghorn, low and long, under the Pre-title card.

Rain on the roof. A walkie-talkie crackles on the bunk. Two walkies charge by the lanturn.

INTERCUT - CABIN AND THE DOCK

Offscreen, a dog barks. Then the voiceover again, over the crossfade.

GRETA (V.O.)
(sotto voce)
Not yet.

We see the jetty from her pov, in slo-mo: a flashforward to the storm.

Walla from the dock. The intercuts quicken; two prelaps, then a slugline's worth of silence.

GRETA (CONT'D)
(cont'd)
Now.

The logline, in a note to herself: [[a sightline across the water]]

